{
  "title": "Hyperswitch \u2014 fintech (42,716\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Hyperswitch\nDomain: fintech | Scale: large | Stars: 42,716\nProblem: Hyperswitch is an open-source, composable payments infrastructure that enables businesses to integrate multiple payment processors, reduce costs through intelligent routing and cost observability, and streamline payment operations without vendor lock-in.\nTarget users: Payment service providers, E-commerce platforms, SaaS companies, Fintech startups, Enterprise merchants\nCore features: Multi-PSP Integration; Intelligent Routing; PCI-Compliant Vault; Revenue Recovery with Retry Strategies; Cost Observability & Analytics; Automated Reconciliation; Alternate Payment Methods\nIntegrations: Stripe, Adyen, Braintree, Worldpay, Checkout.com, PayPal, Apple Pay, Google Pay, Samsung Pay, Klarna, VGS, TokenEx\nTech stack: React, JavaScript, TypeScript, CSS + Rust + PostgreSQL + Docker, Kubernetes-ready\nKey libraries: Newman (API testing), Actix or similar Rust web framework\nArchitecture: microservices\nDesign lessons:\n- Modular design allows customers to adopt individual payment modules independently without full platform lock-in\n- High-performance Rust backend chosen for payment processing reliability, security, and throughput at scale\n- Composable architecture enables integration of 120+ payment processors through pluggable connectors rather than monolithic payment gateway\n- PCI compliance and vault abstraction are first-class architectural concerns, supporting bring-your-own-vault patterns for existing provider integration",
